  Repaint this grey block mockup as a finished video game screenshot of a river trading town. 16-bit SNES pixel art, isometric 2:1 projection, warm earthy palette (browns, tans, terracotta, forest green, stone grey, gold, deep red, sky blue), single dark outline, medium shading, light from the top left, medieval central European, 14th century. Crisp pixels, no blur, no text, no UI. Keep EXACTLY the camera, the position, footprint and height of every building, the streets, the water and the little people: the people are 1.7 m tall adults and set the scale; do not shrink or enlarge any building. The red blocks along the river become tall narrow Hanseatic brick merchant houses with stepped gables and hoist beams; the cream blocks are half-timbered houses; the long grey building with the tower is a gothic church with a slate spire; the big grey block is a stone town hall; the blue band is a river with a stone arched bridge where the street crosses, wooden quays and a wooden harbour crane, moored boats, the cobbled area is the market square with stalls. Add barrels, crates, sacks, carts and many townsfolk.

